{"type":"data","nodes":[null,{"type":"data","data":[{"title":1,"excerpt":2,"tags":3,"film":13},"Tout s'est bien passé (Everything Went Fine)","Emmanuèle, romancière épanouie dans sa vie privée et professionnelle, se précipite à l’hôpital, son père André vient de faire un AVC. Fantasque, aimant passionnément la vie mais diminué, il demande à sa fille de l’aider à en finir. Avec l’aide de sa sœur Pascale, elle va devoir choisir : accepter la volonté de son père ou le convaincre de changer d’avis. (When André, 85, has a stroke, Emmanuèle hurries to her father’s bedside. Sick and half-paralyzed in his hospital bed, he asks Emmanuèle to help him end his life. But how can you honor such a request when it’s your own father?)",[4,5,6,7,8,9,10,11,12],"parenthood","suicide","physical illness","lgbtqi","hospital","cultural memory","agony","may-december","medical treatment",{"type":14,"id":15,"slug":16,"title":17,"release":20,"filmType":24,"directors":25,"genre":45,"media":47,"synopsis":50,"production":53,"characters":56,"roles":84,"awards":142,"tags":3},"Film","FR2021_072","fr2021-072-tout-s-est-bien-passe",{"native":18,"english":19},"Tout s'est bien passé","Everything Went Fine",{"type":21,"date":22,"year":23},"Theatrical release","2021-09-22",2021,"Fiction film",[26],{"id":27,"slug":28,"name":27,"birthYear":29,"deathYear":30,"gender":31,"nationality":32,"awards":33},"François Ozon","francois-ozon",1967,0,"Male identifying","France",[34,39,42],{"film":35,"year":23,"award":36,"category":37,"result":38},"fr2020-045-ete-85","César du cinéma","Best Director","Nominated",{"film":40,"year":41,"award":36,"category":37,"result":38},"fr2019-036-grace-a-dieu",2020,{"film":43,"year":44,"award":36,"category":37,"result":38},"fr2016-126-frantz",2017,[46],"Drama",{"posterUrl":48,"trailerUrl":49},"https://medias.unifrance.org/medias/24/160/237592/format_page/everything-went-fine.jpg","https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=zgBkLyB2MB4",{"native":51,"english":52},"Emmanuèle, romancière épanouie dan